EXPERIMENT 1 — Anaconda, Colab & ML Libraries
Aim
To study platforms such as Anaconda and Google Colab and understand commonly used machine learning libraries.
Theory
- Anaconda: Python distribution containing Python, Jupyter Notebook and data science libraries.
- Google Colab: Cloud-based notebook that executes Python without local installation.
- NumPy: Numerical calculations and arrays.
- Pandas: Data handling and analysis.
- Matplotlib: Graphs and visualization.
- Seaborn: Statistical visualization.
- Scikit-learn: ML algorithms, preprocessing and evaluation.
- TensorFlow/PyTorch: Deep learning.
